# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Collation protocol v4 with bounded segment advertisements

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      This PR adds collation protocol v4 (`/collation/4`). A v4 collator sends one
      `AdvertiseSegment` per scheduling parent and core with up to `MAX_SEGMENT_LEN` (32)
      candidate fingerprints (output head hash, parent head hash, claim queue offset). There is
      no `Declare` and no `CollationSeconded` in v4. The para id is part of the advertisement and
      the peer is bound to it by its first one. Segments are only handled by the experimental
      validator side. The collator side keeps one segment per (scheduling parent, core) and
      drops later ones for the same key. v2/v3 validators get a regular `AdvertiseCollation` for
      the segment tip.

      New request-response protocol `/req_collation/3` (`request_response::v3`). The request
      has scheduling parent, para id and output head data hash instead of relay parent and
      candidate hash. The response always contains the parent head data.

      Collators and validators started with `--experimental-collator-protocol` use v4 as the
      main collation protocol, v3 and v2 are fallbacks. Everything else pins v3 via
      `PeerSetProtocolNames::new_with_main_collation_version`. `PeerSetProtocolNames::new` picks
      the newest supported version now. Nodes running the old validator side have to pin v3 with
      `new_with_main_collation_version`, otherwise v4 gets negotiated with new collators and
      their advertisements are dropped. `/req_collation/3` has to be registered with the network
      like the v2 one and the receiver goes into `OverseerGenArgs::collation_req_v3_receiver` /
      `ProtocolSide::Collator::request_receiver_v3`.

      - `CollationGenerationMessage::SubmitCollation` and `SubmitCollationParams` are replaced by
        `SubmitSegment` and `SubmitSegmentParams`: a list of `SegmentCollation` with one
        scheduling parent, core index and descriptor version for the whole segment. V2 segments
        must have exactly one collation. Only V2 and V3 descriptor versions are accepted.
      - `CollatorProtocolMessage::DistributeCollation` is replaced by `DistributeSegment`
        (`Segment`, `SegmentEntry`), the receipt is assembled in the collator protocol.
      - `CollationResult::result_sender`, `CollationResult::into_inner`,
        `CollationSecondedSignal` and `TryFrom<&CollationSecondedSignal> for BlockAnnounceData`
        are removed. `CollationSeconded` messages from old validators are ignored.
      - `CandidateDescriptorVersion::Unknown` is now `Unknown(u8)`. This changes the encoding of
        the variant, which is part of the v3 `AdvertiseCollation` message but never sent by a
        working node.
      - `CollationProtocols` has a fourth type parameter for `V4`. `Requests` and `Protocol`
        have a new `CollationFetchingV3` variant.
      - `PeerSet::get_main_version()` is removed, use `PeerSetProtocolNames::get_main_version()`.
        `PeerSetProtocolNames::get_fallback_names()` is a method now.
      - `TestCandidateBuilder` has new `scheduling_parent` and `para_head` fields and
        `build_v3()`.
      - `polkadot_primitives::v9::parse_ump_signals_for_commitments` runs the UMP signal checks
        without a receipt.
      - The lookahead collator builds one block per relay parent, the loop building up to two
        is removed.
      - The collator declares with the negotiated protocol version when the authority ids
        arrive after the connection, previously it assumed v2.

      Adds a zombienet test for v3/v4 negotiation with a mixed validator set.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      No action needed. Validators only negotiate v4 with `--experimental-collator-protocol`.
      Collators fall back to v3/v2 for older validators. There is no required upgrade order
      between validators and collators.

